export anchor RetroGrooveStyle:
    number: 286
    screen: CodeRepository
    name: Retro groove
    idea: A warm brown-black conversation timeline with a three-stripe orange, mustard and aqua band, slab serif headings, chunky pill buttons with hard offset shadows and a ticket stub side column, like a seventies hi-fi brochure set in code.
    base: dark
    palette:
        espresso: #1f1a16, the page background and the diff code area
        walnut: #2b241e, timeline cards, the side tickets and the style sheet cards
        cocoa: #3a3028, the masthead, chips, the hunk header and the disabled merge button
        grain: #5c4c3d, borders, the timeline spine and dashed ticket tears
        cream: #f3e6c9, text
        sand: #cdb994, meta, line numbers and side labels
        tangerine: #fe8a3c, the primary button, slab headings, the current tab and focus
        mustard: #f5c046, requested changes and the middle stripe
        aqua: #8ec9b0, links and the third stripe
        olive: #b8cc5a, passed, approved, Open and added lines
        brick: #f47a6c, failing and removed lines
        shadow: #0e0b09, the hard 4px offset shadow under buttons and cards
        addTint: #2c3220, added line rows
        delTint: #3d2420, removed line rows
    type:
        Headings in a slab serif stack, Rockwell, Roboto Slab, Zilla Slab, DejaVu
        Serif, Georgia, title 32px at 700 and section titles 20px. Body in Trebuchet
        MS, Segoe UI, system-ui at 15px on 1.55. Ticket labels 12px caps tracked
        0.14em. Code in Courier New, ui-monospace at 14px.
    layout:
        A cocoa masthead with a round B badge, the owner and repository in slab
        type, a Private stamp and Watch 12, Star 48 and Fork 3 as small pills.
        Directly under it a band of three 6px stripes in tangerine, mustard and aqua
        runs the full width. Tabs follow as rounded top folders, the current one
        tangerine. The title block sits at 1140px. Below, two columns. The left is a
        vertical timeline with a 2px grain spine and round nodes holding icons, with
        events for Sam Ortiz opening the request, the three changed files, the
        checks result with e2e-android named, Jonas Weber approving, and Tomás Ruiz
        requesting changes with the diff card and inline comment nested in his
        event. The right is a 300px stack of ticket stubs with dashed tear lines for
        assignees, labels, milestone, linked issue and the merge stub. Below 900px
        the tickets move under the timeline.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 20px card padding, 24px between timeline events, 48px timeline indent.
    density: Medium low. A story told top to bottom, one event at a time.
    corners: Round and chunky. 14px cards, 999px buttons, tabs and chips, round timeline nodes.
    borders: 2px grain borders on cards and tickets, dashed 2px tear lines between ticket sections, a 2px spine.
    shadows: Hard 4px by 4px offset shadows in near black under cards and buttons, no blur.
    icons:
        Line icons at 2.25px stroke inside 32px round timeline nodes and inline at
        1.1em. Check circle for passed and approved, crossed square for failing,
        triangle with a bang for requested changes, padlock for the blocked merge.
    focus: A 3px tangerine outline offset 3px.
    tone: Friendly and narrative, such as Sam Ortiz opened this pull request and Tomás Ruiz asked for changes.
